#, kde-kuit-format
#~ msgctxt "@info"
#~ msgid ""
#~ "This type of backup is an <emphasis>archive</emphasis>. It contains both the latest version of your files and earlier backed up versions. Using this type of backup allows you to recover older versions of your files, or files which were deleted on your computer at a later time. The storage space needed is minimized by looking for common parts of your files between versions and only storing those parts once. Nevertheless, the backup archive will keep growing in size as time goes by.<nl/>"
#~ "Also important to know is that the files in the archive can not be accessed directly with a general file manager, a special program is needed."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "O tipo de salvagarda é un <emphasis>arquivo</emphasis>. Contén tanto a última versión dos ficheiros como as versións anteriores salvagardadas. Usar este tipo de salvagarda permite recuperar versións anteriores dos ficheiros, ou ficheiros que eliminou posteriormente do computador. O espazo de almacenamento necesario minimízase buscando as partes comúns dos ficheiros e almacenándoas unha única vez. Porén, o arquivo de salvagarda medrará constantemente co paso do tempo.<nl/>"
#~ "Tamén cómpre ter en conta que non é posíbel acceder directamente aos ficheiros do arquivo cun xestor de ficheiros xeral, necesítase un programa especial."

#, kde-kuit-format
#~ msgctxt "@info"
#~ msgid ""
#~ "This type of backup is a folder which is synchronized with your selected source folders. Saving a backup simply means making the backup destination contain an exact copy of your source folders as they are now and nothing else. If a file has been deleted in a source folder it will get deleted from the backup folder.<nl/>"
#~ "This type of backup can protect you against data loss due to a broken hard drive but it does not help you to recover from your own mistakes."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Este tipo de salvagarda é un cartafol que se sincroniza cos cartafoles de orixe seleccionados. Salvagardar significa simplemente facer que o destino da salvagarda conteña unha copia exacta dos cartafoles de orixe no seu estado actual, máis nada. Se un ficheiro se elimina dun cartafol de orixe, eliminarase do cartafol de salvagarda.<nl/>"
#~ " Este tipo de salvagarda pode protexer de perdas de datos causadas por roturas de disco duro, pero non polas causadas accidentalmente por vostede."
